WEBVTT

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:05.533
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> <b>The Glass Bottle. Part 1</b>

00:00:14.595 --> 00:00:17.156
Hassan and Walid are brothers.

00:00:17.862 --> 00:00:25.423
They live in a small house in the desert, near the mountains, a long way from a town or village.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:32.523
They’re very poor. They have no money and they have no animals.

00:00:33.502 --> 00:00:39.513
Their house only has two rooms. Every day is the same.

00:00:40.223 --> 00:00:44.879
They get up, and they have sweet black coffee for breakfast.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.546
Then Hassan works in the fields –

00:00:49.225 --> 00:00:56.713
but Walid just sits and looks at the hot, empty desert and the hot, empty sky.

00:00:57.716 --> 00:01:05.036
They live with their mother. She takes care of them, but she’s old and tired.

00:01:06.244 --> 00:01:14.736
One day she says, "We’re poor and hungry. Why don’t you leave here and find work?

00:01:15.092 --> 00:01:18.203
We need money for food and clothes."

00:01:19.858 --> 00:01:28.669
"If you want some money, you have your silver ring – you can sell that," answers Walid.

00:01:29.827 --> 00:01:40.440
"I can’t sell it," she says. "It’s your father’s. Every night I look at it and remember him."

00:01:41.845 --> 00:01:47.306
Hassan wants to help his mother, and he decides to leave home.

00:01:48.177 --> 00:01:52.673
His mother gives him bread, and water in a glass bottle.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:57.706
He kisses her, and he walks towards the mountains.